On Apr 10, 8:46 pm, "Jimlock3000" <james.m.schm...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I just ended my best game so far (chaotic human barbarian XP 14 DL
> Valley of the Dead), and have two questions for experts, and one piece
> of advice for new folks:
>
> Question 1.  Once I beat the Mines and Sokoban (first time for either
> one, let alone both), the main dungeon got a LOT easier--the next
> 15-20 levels were a breeze.  Is this usually the case?
>

OH YES. First, the mines are great for improving AC. It's quite easy
to get your AC to -5 or less by carrying away the iron shoes, helms,
roundshields, and armor coats of your gnomish/dwarvish quarry from the
mines, then price-Id'ing them for enchantment, especially if you're a
Combat Wombat and therefore have high strength and little/no concern
about the drawbacks of metal armor. My priest characters, who can try
on armor as they kill enemies due to intrinsic B/U/C detection, can
easily obtain AC of -10 without delving far past Minetown. However,
since none of my priests have gotten much farther due to poor
weaponry, it's pretty clear that high AC isn't everything. If a
character has no offensive ability, he can still be overwhelmed by
swarms of monsters.

Furthermore, that Bag of Holding from Sokoban has always make a great
difference to me, simply because I'm such a packrat and like to play
casters with poor strength.

> Question 2.  I gave all my pocket change (the $140 I was carrying) to
> the Priestess of Gehennom in the Valley of the Dead, and she went
> berserk and killed me.  What gives?
>

The priest's behavior strikes me as strange. According to the source
code, the only ways to anger a priest besides hitting him are to wake
him while sleeping or to
desecrate his altar. If you woke him while sleeping, you'd get one of
the following messages:

424.  		"Thou wouldst have words, eh?  I'll give thee a word or two!",
425.  		"Talk?  Here is what I have to say!",
426.  		"Pilgrim, I would speak no longer with thee."

And if you desecrated the altar, you'd get

443.  	    verbalize("Begone!  Thou desecratest this holy place with
thy presence.");

If you donate between 0-200xExperience, the priest is supposed to call
you a cheapskate, but not become hostile.

> Advice 1 (and Only).  Don't pick a fight with a Priest when you're XP
> level 7, unless you really know what you're doing.  (I didn't!)

Yep. Polymorph your pet into something buff and have *him* kill the
priest to avoid loss of protection/murder penalties. I use a magic
whistle and poly traps to polymorph my pets at mines' end, where poly
traps are common. Barring that, use a wand/potion of polymorph to turn
the priest into the High and Exalted Grid Bug of (insert deity)
first. ;)



